    "https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8796": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "Ashland University Portal | Full-Time Salad Prep - Student Dining Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Ashland University Home Human Resources Home Full-Time Salad Prep - Student Dining Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Full-Time Salad Prep - Student Dining Job Description Covers days off for other employees. Schedule will vary from a.m. to p.m. along with every other weekend. Duties include vegetable prep, salad composition, assembling catering trays and salads. Stocks and maintains raw ingredients for Student Dining salad bar. May be required to work other positions based on staffing needs. Required Qualifications HIgh volume production facility. Performs the duties in an efficient and positive manner, meeting the objectives of Ashland University. Follows state health department guidelines and dress codes. Applicant must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Ashland University will not sponsor or take over sponsorship for an employment visa. Preferred Qualifications Excellent knife skills with high production. Serv Safe certified. Physical Demands Standing long periods. Able to lift up to 40 lbs. Temperature changes from cooler to the kitchen. Anticipated Start Date of New Hire 09/07/2026 Anticipated Number of Hours Working per Week 40 Shift Required? Varied Job Duties Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1139P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 09/07/2026 Job Open Date 08/31/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8795 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents 401 College Avenue Ashland, OH 44805 419.289.4142, 800.882.1548 Athletics Employment Commencement News Center Accessibility Bac