    "https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8694": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "Ashland University Portal | Sales and Marketing Manager, Catering and Conferences Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Ashland University Home Human Resources Home Sales and Marketing Manager, Catering and Conferences Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Sales and Marketing Manager, Catering and Conferences Job Description The Ashland University Catering and Conferences Sales and Marketing Manager will work directly with clients and potential clients to secure their business and plan events. This position will also work with internal AU clients to generate BEOs for their events. This position is also responsible for all print and digital marketing for Catering and Conferences including brochures, menus, website, social media, and email campaigns. Sales Responsibilities ·Lead venue tours with prospective clients. Initiate and complete all sales follow-up for all leads including emails, calls, and reminders, including tracking in ClickUp. Generate all food, beverages, linen, and décor details for all their booked events. Manage all upselling and cross-selling programs, including décor, all-inclusive packages, and Eagle Custom merchandise. Manage the AU Catering email account with the Director and respond to all catering inquiries received, excluding campus and conference inquiries. Receive and respond to all website inquiries, excluding conference inquiries. Attend bridal shows to promote AU Catering services and event venues. Work with the Director and Chef to plan special university-hosted events such as YMBC Ladies Night, the Eagler Golf Outing, and other assigned events. Collaborate with the Director of Catering and Conferences to develop new menus, packages, brochures, and pricing. Generate all internal supply orders and maintain the supply order form with new items and annual pricing updates. Coordinate repeat client bookings from year to year or for multi-year agreements. Coordinate and conduct bridal and other large event tastings. Support sales and marketing initiatives across other Auxiliary Services departments. Propose and review approved quarterly Key Performance Indicators (KPIs). Marketing Responsibilities Create marketing materials and campaigns for catering special events, menus, brochures, and social media content consistent with Ashland University brand guidelines. Manage the Catering website. Manage all digital marketing content, including Catering Instagram, Facebook, and wedding/event website pages. Design and produce both digital and print marketing materials. Create and distribute all catering email marketing campaigns. Conduct post-event follow-up with large event clients to gather feedback. Other Responsibilities Generate Contracts for all external sold events. Be present at the more demanding events sold like weddings and big conferences, at least until meal is served. During summer seasons, assist the Director with Conference logistics when needed. Review invoices weekly to confirm final client charges. Submit RSVP reminders for upcoming clients. Receive deposits and payments as needed when the Director is unavailable. Place Connie Douglin Linen orders for booked events. Supervise and direct event supervisors, setup workers, and other catering staff. Required Qualifications Experience in a food service operation. Experience in event management. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in business administration, Hospitality, or Marketing. Physical Demands Be able to move throughout campus for extended periods while conducting client meetings, facility tours, and overseeing catering and conference events. The position requires occasional bending, reaching, lifting, carrying, pushing or pulling up to 25 lbs., and up to 40-50 lbs. with assistance. Ability to operate computers, office equipment, and audiovisual technology. Flexibility to work some evenings, weekends, holidays, and both indoor and outdoor events as business needs require. Anticipated Start Date of New Hire 08/31/2026 Anticipated Number of Hours Working per Week 40-50 Shift Required? Varied Job Duties Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1127P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 08/31/2026 Job Open Date 08/06/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8693 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letters Of Recommendation 401 College Avenue Ashland, OH 44805 419.289.4142, 800.882.1548 Athletics Employment Commencement News Center Accessibility Back to top Wellness Consumer Information Student Complaints Campus Store To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
