    "https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8797": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "Ashland University Portal | Desktop Engineer - Information Technology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Ashland University Home Human Resources Home Desktop Engineer - Information Technology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Desktop Engineer - Information Technology Job Description The Desktop Engineer is a forward-thinking IT professional responsible for ensuring optimal desktop and endpoint operations across our diverse environment. This role not only covers traditional desktop support but also integrates modern endpoint management practices including cloud and mobile device management ( MDM ), cybersecurity fundamentals, and server-level administration. The successful candidate will be proficient in managing environments that leverage tools such as Microsoft Intune, Autopilot, JAMF for Apple device management, and traditional systems like Active Directory, Entra, and Azure. They will work collaboratively with IT peers, security teams, and client services to ensure that computer images, software deployments, and system customizations meet the highest standards of reliability, scalability, and security, in line with NIST guidelines and industry best practices. Desktop and Endpoint Management Create, maintain, and deploy modern computer images for Windows and Mac OS environments. Manage and update endpoint devices using both traditional systems (e.g., Jira, JAMF ) and modern cloud-based tools (e.g., Microsoft Intune). Manage Windows Autopilot Oversee mobile device management ( MDM ) practices to ensure secure and efficient management of enterprise mobile devices. Cloud and Server Administration Manage cloud applications and enforce cloud app security protocols. Execute lower-level system administrator duties, including server patching, customizations, and routine maintenance. Administer and maintain Active Directory, Entra, and Azure environments to support organizational infrastructure. Help support the Hyper-V server environment and infrastructure. Cybersecurity and Compliance Integrate cybersecurity practices into daily operations, ensuring compliance with NIST standards and industry best practices. Collaborate with cybersecurity teams to implement machine hardening, secure patching, and proactive vulnerability management. Automation, Scripting, and System Updates Develop and execute scripts (using PowerShell and other scripting languages) to automate routine tasks and OS setting adjustments. Maintain a comprehensive update schedule for operating systems and applications, ensuring timely patching and customization. Technical Support and Documentation Respond to user tickets regarding software deployment, device management, and system updates, providing excellent end-user support. Analyze the impact of proposed technology changes and document policies, procedures, and technical guides. Train and mentor junior IT staff, serving as a role model and technical resource within the team. Cross-Functional Collaboration and Process Improvement Work closely with IT support, security, networking, and other project teams to develop and implement scalable technology solutions. Identify and recommend process improvements to enhance the overall efficiency, security, and reliability of IT operations. Foster strong working relationships with stakeholders, ensuring that IT solutions align with both business and educational objectives. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, or a related field, plus three (3) years of relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of education, certification, and experience. At least three (3) years of customer service experience. Proven ability to work effectively in project teams and manage multiple initiatives concurrently. Applicant must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Ashland University will not sponsor or take over sponsorship for an employment visa. Preferred Qualifications Certifications related to workstation management, cybersecurity, networking, and customer service (e.g., A+, Security+, Network+, Azure Fundamentals, Microsoft Certifications, Apple Certifications, etc.). Experience with endpoint management appliances such as Intune and JAMF . Prior experience in an educational environment or similar setting. Familiarity with cloud management platforms, mobile device management ( MDM ), and enterprise server management. Background in operating systems administration (Windows, Mac OS) and software deployment (Adobe, MS Office, utilities, etc.). Exposure to cybersecurity best practices and compliance standards (e.g., NIST ). Proficiency in managing and troubleshooting various operating systems and platforms. Strong analytical skills with the ability to assess and implement system improvements. Excellent communication and technical writing abilities. Capacity to balance multiple projects and priorities in a dynamic environment. Ability to mentor and support junior IT personnel. Experience with scripting and automation tools (e.g., PowerShell). Physical Demands Work is performed in an office environment with occasional lifting and hauling of equipment up to sixty (60) lbs. Standard work hours are 8AM – 5PM with opportunities for hybrid/remote work. A valid Driver’s License and the ability to travel to remote campus locations and attend training sessions are required. Anticipated Start Date of New Hire 10/01/2026 Anticipated Number of Hours Working per Week 40 Shift Required? First Job Duties Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1136P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 10/01/2026 Job Open Date 08/28/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8779 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letters Of Recommendation 401 College Avenue Ashland, OH 44805 419.289.4142, 800.882.1548 Athletics Employment Commencement News Center Accessibility Back to top Wellness Consumer Information Student Complaints Campus Store To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8695": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "Ashland University Portal | Full-Time Building Service Worker - Building Services Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Ashland University Home Human Resources Home Full-Time Building Service Worker - Building Services Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Full-Time Building Service Worker - Building Services Job Description Cleaning and maintaining living facilities, dining areas, laundry areas, restrooms, shower areas, classrooms and offices. Replenishing soap and paper products. Removing trash and recycling from buildings while replacing liners in the trash and recycling containers. Sweeping, mopping and cleaning floors and stairwells. Vacuuming and shampooing carpeted areas. Dusting furniture, washing walls and windows. Cleaning outside steps and entryways (may include snow removal from entryways). Moving heavy furniture, supplies and equipment. Burnishing, refinishing and stripping tile and terrazzo flooring. Reporting items in need of repair and ordering supplies. Performing related or special duties as assigned by a supervisor. Required Qualifications Must be dependable, trustworthy, flexible and a team player. Able to work effectively in an environment subject to frequently changing priorities. Ability to operate power equipment (vacuum cleaners, carpet extractors, high and low speed burnishers, auto scrubbers and other possible equipment used in connection with building cleaning). Applicant must have reliable transportation. Attention to detail is critical.Availability to work weekends as needed. Applicant must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Ashland University will not sponsor or take over sponsorship for an employment visa. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Exposure to external temperatures during the cleaning of entrances or around the perimeter of the building and exposure to heat/humidity during summer months. Ability to lift boxes, trash, ladders and equipment. Ability to perform tasks in high, low and confined spaces. Exposure to chemicals in cleaning products, dust, dirt and germs. Anticipated Start Date of New Hire 08/17/2026 Anticipated Number of Hours Working per Week 40 Shift Required? First Job Duties Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1125P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 08/17/2026 Job Open Date 08/06/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8688 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents 401 College Avenue Ashland, OH 44805 419.289.4142, 800.882.1548 Athletics Employment Commencement News Center Accessibility Back to top Wellness Consumer Information Student Complaints Campus Store To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8826": {
      "title": "Part-Time Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Ashland University Portal | Part-Time Administrative Assistant - Ashbrook Center Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Ashland University Home Human Resources Home Part-Time Administrative Assistant - Ashbrook Center Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Part-Time Administrative Assistant - Ashbrook Center Job Description We are seeking a dependable, organized, and proactive Part-Time Administrative Assistant to support the day-to-day operations of the Ashbrook Center. The ideal candidate is a self-starter who can work independently, prioritize responsibilities, and provide professional and welcoming support to staff, interns, and visitors. Duties include, but are not limited to: Answer the main phone line, take messages, and disseminate information to appropriate staff. Order office and kitchen supplies and monitor inventory levels to ensure needed items are available. Monitor interns and assist with assigning and coordinating their workload. Welcome and assist visitors by providing directions, answering questions, and connecting them with appropriate personnel. Manage incoming and outgoing USPS mail and UPS packages. Work with related departments to execute tasks and provide administrative support as needed. Ensure the smooth and efficient operation of the Ashbrook workroom and intern suite. Perform other administrative duties and special projects as assigned. Required Qualifications Two plus (2+) years professional office experience required. Detail oriented, self-motivated and able to take initiative with minimal supervision. Strong organizational and time-management skills. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Professional, friendly, and dependable demeanor. Ability to prioritize multiple tasks and work effectively in an active office environment. Comfortable working with staff, interns, visitors, and colleagues across departments. Knowledge of general office software and equipment usage. Experience in non-profit fundraising or marketing experience a plus, but no prior experience in these fields is required. Applicant must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Ashland University will not sponsor or take over sponsorship for an employment visa. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Anticipated Start Date of New Hire 10/01/2026 Anticipated Number of Hours Working per Week 25 Shift Required? First Job Duties Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1142P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 10/01/2026 Job Open Date 09/02/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8825 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letters Of Recommendation 401 College Avenue Ashland, OH 44805 419.289.4142, 800.882.1548 Athletics Employment Commencement News Center Accessibility Back to top Wellness Consumer Information Student Complaints Campus Store To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
