    "https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8844": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "Ashland University Portal | Part-Time Catering Cook - Catering and Conferences Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Ashland University Home Human Resources Home Part-Time Catering Cook - Catering and Conferences Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Part-Time Catering Cook - Catering and Conferences Job Description Assist catering chef with production and service of catered events on and off campus. Hours are varied due to timing of catered events. Part-time position eligible for vacation, sick, and holiday pay. Required Qualifications Previous cooking experience in a large volume operation. Knowledge of food safety. Applicant must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Ashland University will not sponsor or take over sponsorship for an employment visa. Preferred Qualifications High School diploma or equivalent. ServSafe certification. Physical Demands Lifting and standing for long periods at a time. Anticipated Start Date of New Hire 09/14/2026 Anticipated Number of Hours Working per Week 29 Shift Required? Varied Job Duties Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1146P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 09/14/2026 Job Open Date 09/04/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8843 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents 401 College Avenue Ashland, OH 44805 419.289.4142, 800.882.1548 Athletics Employment Commencement News Center Accessibility Back to top Wellness Consumer Information Student Complaints Campus Store To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
