    "https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8438": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "Ashland University Portal | Nurse Practitioner - Student Health Center Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Ashland University Home Human Resources Home Nurse Practitioner - Student Health Center Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Nurse Practitioner - Student Health Center Job Description This primary care provider works collaboratively with a multidisciplinary team responsible for the provision of quality health care services for students of Ashland University in accordance with standards of professional practice and ethical conduct. This team member provides clinical assessment, diagnosis and treatment for Ashland University students who are seen as patients in the Student Health Center. This is a 9-month position with full-time benefits. Assume ongoing responsibility for the primary care of Ashland University students’ health needs. Provide diagnosis, treatment and follow-up management of common acute illness and injuries and management of stable chronic conditions. Promote health and wellness in areas of lifestyle and behavior that enhance physical, psychological, spiritual and social well-being. Document appropriate, accurate and complete information in the student’s medical record, in accordance with current Student Health Center policies and procedures. Consult with his/her collaborating/supervising physician in an appropriate and timely manner when indicated or required by law. Refer students to collaborating/supervising physician, other health care providers or relevant community agencies, when indicated. Serve as preceptor for Athletic Training students. Provide evaluation, treatment and/or referral of employee occupational injuries. Maintain strict confidentiality of clinical, social, financial or other student/staff data in compliance with university, state and federal guidelines. Communicate effectively with students, parents, physicians and colleagues. Seek opportunities to promote professional and personal growth through available continuing educational activities. Review and maintain Standard Care Arrangement/Physician Supervisory Plan with collaborating/supervising physician on an annual basis (or as required by law). Demonstrate behavior which reflects a positive image of the Student Health Center and the University. Demonstrate team member behaviors. Serve on division and institution-wide committees as assigned. Required Qualifications Master’s degree required as per certification. Three (3) to five (5) years primary care experience. Licensed to practice and prescribe in the State of Ohio. Certification in his/her specialty by a nationally recognized certification board. Education and training as an Advanced Practice Nurse/Physician Assistant required. Experience in providing telehealth services. Ability to work flexible hours. Ability to handle and prioritize diverse tasks. Strong communication skills. Excellent clinical skills. Applicant must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Ashland University will not sponsor or take over sponsorship for an employment visa. Preferred Qualifications Advanced Practice Nurse, certification in Adult or Family Health preferred. At least one (1) year College Health experience preferred. Experience in sports medicine/orthopedics and/or women’s health preferred. Physical Demands Able to bend and reach as required for patient care. Potential exposure to infectious disease and biohazardous materials. Exposure to stress in busy office environment, dealing with difficult/unhappy customers. Anticipated Start Date of New Hire 08/03/2026 Anticipated Number of Hours Working per Week 40 Shift Required? First Job Duties Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1069P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 08/03/2026 Job Open Date 05/06/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8241 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter References 401 College Avenue Ashland, OH 44805 419.289.4142, 800.882.1548 Athletics Employment Commencement News Center Accessibility Back to top Wellness Consumer Information Student Complaints Campus Store To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
