    "https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8735": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biblical Studies",
      "description": "Ashland University Portal | Assistant Professor of Biblical Studies - Ashland Theological Seminary Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Ashland University Home Human Resources Home Assistant Professor of Biblical Studies - Ashland Theological Seminary Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please provide a letter of application, curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts, teaching philosophy, and a Statement of Faith. Three (3) professional references are also required including name, email, and phone number. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor of Biblical Studies - Ashland Theological Seminary Division Ashland Theological Seminary (ATS) Department Seminary Job Description Ashland Theological Seminary ( ATS ) is a graduate division of Ashland University, located in Ashland, Ohio. The position is a full-time, tenure-track faculty position in Biblical Studies. This nine-month position begins on August 23, 2027 . Ethos of Ashland Theological Seminary ATS was founded by the Brethren Church, whose Anabaptist and Pietist heritage shapes the core values of the Seminary. The Seminary is an evangelical and ecumenical institution, as well as a community of faith whose identity is shaped by its service to the scholarly community, the church, and the world. We embrace a diversity that finds its unity in Jesus Christ. We are committed to practicing justice in our engagement with one another and with the world. As partners in ministry and brothers and sisters in Christ, we strive to foster a redemptive community that lives by the values of God’s kingdom. Agreement with the Seminary’s Statement of Faith, Mission, Strategic Vision, and Ethos statement is required. Candidate will demonstrate competence in the study and teaching of the Hebrew Bible, including but not limited to hermeneutics, exegesis, and Biblical Hebrew language. Teach and advise students in Seminary courses in Biblical Studies, provide academic oversight of students, will pursue scholarly and professional development, serve on departmental and Seminary committees as needed, and work collegially with Seminary faculty and local stakeholders. Candidate will demonstrate a commitment to support and respect the Brethren Church heritage, commit to theological education delivered from a Christ-centered worldview, express a strong commitment to a servant-leadership model. Deliver courses in multiple formats, whether in-person, hybrid, fully online, or intensive. Courses may be scheduled during the daytime, evenings, and/or weekends. Expected to participate in all relevant Seminary student and faculty academic activities. Represent the Seminary and engage in community activities that promote theological education and Christian practices. Required Qualifications PhD in Hebrew Bible or cognate discipline. Record of successful experience in higher education and/or other educational environments. (experience teaching in non-traditional formats, hybrid and/or online courses preferable) Track record as a collaborative servant-leader with outstanding skills in written and verbal communication and in interpersonal relationships. Active participation in the life of the Church. Leadership experience in Christian ministry. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Anticipated Start Date of New Hire 08/23/2027 Proposed Rank Assistant Tenure-Track No Service Basis 9 month Fixed Term Yes Term Start Date 08/23/2027 Term End Date 05/12/2028 Benefits Yes Job Duties Posting Detail Information Posting Number F127P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 08/23/2027 Job Open Date 08/19/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Please provide a letter of application, curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts, teaching philosophy, and a Statement of Faith. Three (3) professional references are also required including name, email, and phone number. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Quick Link for Postings https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8734 Reference Collection References Minimum Requests Maximum Requests Recommendation Deadline Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Teaching Statement Unofficial Transcripts References Statement of Faith Optional Documents Letters Of Recommendation 401 College Avenue Ashland, OH 44805 419.289.4142, 800.882.1548 Athletics Employment Commencement News Center Accessibility Back to top Wellness Consumer Information Student Complaints Campus Store To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
